---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { links } from '../config';

/*
 * The one page on the site written in the first person.
 *
 * Everywhere else explains the product; this explains the people. Different
 * job, so a different voice: past tense, "we wondered", the things that went
 * wrong left in. The bench-week details are lifted from docs/roadmap.md's
 * "What live testing taught us" -- they are the texture that makes it read as
 * something that actually happened, because it did.
 *
 * Nothing invented. Every specific here traces to the repo.
 */
---

<Layout
  title="Why"
  description="Why DocSigner exists: no open-source tool would sign with a DSC token, and the first week on a real bench taught us why that is harder than it looks."
>
  <Hero kicker="Why" title="Why we built this" lede="Short version: no tool would do it." />

  <Section ground="deep">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        We are commerce graduates. Accountants, mostly, who liked software more
        than we expected to and taught ourselves to build it. These days that
        means Frappe and ERPNext, and compliance work for people who file the
        same returns we used to file.
      </p>
      <p>
        Which is how we kept arriving at the same wall. Almost everything we
        built ended at a document nobody would accept until it had been signed,
        and in India that means a DSC on a USB token. Everyone doing this work
        has one in a drawer. None of us had a decent way to use it.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we went looking properly. Every tool that handled tokens was
        commercial, or Windows-only, or both. The open-source ones signed
        happily with a key in a file, which is not where a DSC lives. That left
        paying, rebooting into Windows, or printing the page and signing it by
        hand.
      </p>
      <p class="pull">We wondered how hard it could really be.</p>
      <p>
        Harder than it looks. Though almost none of the hard part turned out to
        be cryptography.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="The first week" title="What a real token taught us">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        It worked against test keys long before it worked against hardware. Then
        we plugged in a real Capricorn token, and the list of things we had wrong
        got long quickly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="lessons">
      <li>
        <h3>An empty list has to explain itself</h3>
        <p>
          Ours said “plug in your token” no matter what was actually wrong. That
          cost an afternoon of guessing.
        </p>
        <p class="fix">
          It reports the readers it can see now, so “no token” and “token with no
          driver” read differently.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Token drivers wedge</h3>
        <p>
          The ePass and ProxKey families let exactly one process talk to the token
          at a time, and some only list certificates at the moment they are
          initialised.
        </p>
        <p class="fix">
          So it re-initialises on every scan, gives each driver twenty seconds,
          and names the program you need to close.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Ten handwriting fonts was nine too many</h3>
        <p>Nobody wants to audition ten fonts to sign an invoice.</p>
        <p class="fix">Five now, one per personality.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="after">
      None of that is in a specification. You find it by plugging the thing in,
      which is the only reason it is worth writing down.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section ground="deep" label="One more reason" title="The paper">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        We used to print documents that were born digital, sign them by hand,
        scan them back, and send the scan. Every step made the file worse. That
        was the part that bothered us most.
      </p>
      <p class="after">
        A page printed to be signed and scanned back is a page that should never
        have left the screen.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section centre>
    <div class="end">
      <h2>All of it is Apache-2.0</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Including the parts that touch your token. Read it before you run it.
      </p>
      <div class="row">
        <Button href="/download" variant="primary" size="lg">Download</Button>
        <Button href={links.repo} variant="default" size="lg" trailing="lucide:external-link">
          Read the source
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    max-width: 60ch;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  /* One line gets to be the turn in the story. */
  .pull {
    font-size: var(--display-3);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    margin-block: var(--s-2);
  }

  .lessons {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: l;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
  }

  .lessons li {
    counter-increment: l;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 26px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s-1) var(--s-3);
  }

  /* Every child in the second column, or auto-placement puts the second one
     back under the counter and wraps it a word per line. */
  .lessons li > * {
    grid-column: 2;
  }

  .lessons li::before {
    content: counter(l);
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    border-radius: var(--pill);
    background: var(--green-soft);
    color: var(--green-ink);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .lessons h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-1);
  }

  .lessons p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  /* What we did about it, marked so the list scans as problem then fix. */
  .fix {
    margin-top: var(--s-2);
    padding-left: var(--s-3);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--green);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .after {
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
    padding-left: var(--s-4);
    border-left: var(--accent-bar) solid var(--green);
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .end {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }

  .row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    justify-content: center;
  }
</style>
